#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:111
msgid "Core Concept 1: Quantum-Classical Hybrid Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:113
msgid ""
"KPP follows the standard energy-based model training loop, with a quantum-"
"accelerated negative phase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:115
msgid "Three-Step Training Cycle:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:117
msgid "**Positive Phase (PyTorch, CPU/GPU):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:118
msgid "Compute hidden layer representations from training data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:119
msgid "`h = rbm.get_hidden(x)` → data statistics, no sampling needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:121
msgid "**Negative Phase (Offloaded to SDK):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:122
msgid "Generate samples from the model distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:123
msgid "`s = rbm.sample(sampler)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:124
msgid ""
"Internally, `_to_ising_matrix()` prepares the J/h matrix and dispatches it "
"to a **CIM** (quantum) or **SA** (classical) solver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:126
msgid "**Parameter Update (PyTorch, CPU/GPU):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:127
msgid "`objective = rbm.objective(h, s)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:128
msgid "`objective.backward()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:129
msgid "`optimizer.step()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:185
msgid ""
"**Key Insight:** The only quantum part is `rbm.sample(sampler)`. Everything "
"else is standard PyTorch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:187
msgid "Core Concept 2: Energy Model Hierarchy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/introduction.md:189
msgid ""
"KPP provides a structured class hierarchy. All models share "
"`sample(sampler)` and `objective(h, s)` interfaces."
msgstr ""

